//! From a LENGTH invariant to a SLOT invariant.
//!
//! `iota_immune_of_bvar_major` is pinned by an exact length equation, which
//! forces the bvar to be the **last** argument. That is the only thing the
//! equation buys — and it is exactly what excluded the over-applied case.
//!
//! A slot invariant — `list_head (list_drop MAJOR_IDX (kapp_args x)) = some
//! (bvar i)` — buys the same locating power, is **stable under appending**, and
//! is what `iota_reduct` actually reads.
//!
//! Nine of the eleven preservation arms came out SIMPLER than the length-pinned
//! original, because the invariant is stated on the source's own head rather
//! than on a decomposition: `beta` no longer needs `app_inj_fst`, and
//! `iota`/`delta` need no transports at all. The new cost is confined to the
//! `app` arm.
//!
//! # What this does NOT do
//!
//! It does not discharge `over_res` at its stated type, and the reason is worth
//! recording. `over_res` constrains only the SPINE — dead recursor head, length
//! past the major — and never names what sits in the major slot. `nf_head`'s
//! only usable arm there wants `iota_immune`, a statement over ALL
//! `par_reduces_cd_star` reducts, and every in-tree supplier of that works by
//! exhibiting a SYNTACTIC invariant on the major. With the major arbitrary, the
//! only handle is `wh3_stuck_at`, which speaks about one step at one budget.
//!
//! So `over_res` is strictly **harder** than `bnd_res`, which at least pins its
//! major and hands you `kexpr_top_not_bvar`.
//!
//! # The next brick, precisely
//!
//! A "the slot is inhabited" lemma —
//! `Le (succ k) (list_length xs) -> (forall w, list_head (list_drop k xs) = some w -> C) -> C`
//! (only its converse, `list_head_drop_some_le_succ`, exists). With it, a
//! nine-arm convoy on the recovered major splits `over_res` into the bvar row
//! (discharged here) and a residual that is the exact twin of `bnd_res` — at
//! which point **the two open premises collapse into one**, and that one is the
//! stuck-major confluence argument.
//!
//! `DerivedProved`, empty axiom closures.

use crate::spec::error::SpecError;
use crate::spec::Specification;

impl Specification {
    /// The slot invariant, its preservation, and the over-applied bvar class.
    pub(super) fn add_bvar_slot(&mut self) -> Result<(), SpecError> {
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_KAPP_SLOT_AT_BOUNDARY,
            "kapp_slot_at_boundary: at the exact boundary length, the major IS the last argument. Generalises a closure that was private to stuck_recursor.rs. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_KAPP_MAJOR_SLOT_APP,
            "kapp_major_slot_app: appending an argument does NOT move the major slot. THE STABILITY THE WHOLE GENERALISATION TURNS ON, and it needs no Le hypothesis at all — a thin kapp_args-level wrapper on the existing list_head_drop_append_some. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_KAPP_MAJOR_SLOT_APP_INV,
            "kapp_major_slot_app_inv: the converse, wrapping list_head_drop_append_some_inv. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_LE_SLOT_APP,
            "le_slot_app: the over-applied bound survives appending. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_LE_MI_OF_APP,
            "le_mi_of_app: and descends to the function part. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_BVAR_SLOT_STEP_BOUNDARY,
            "bvar_slot_step_boundary: the app arm's boundary branch, factored out so it DELEGATES to the existing bvar_major_preserved_cd rather than duplicating it. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_BVAR_SLOT_PRESERVED_CD,
            "bvar_slot_preserved_cd: THE SLOT-INVARIANT GENERALISATION. One par_reduces_cd step preserves head-deadness, the over-applied bound, AND a bvar sitting at the major SLOT. \\
\\
iota_immune_of_bvar_major is pinned by an EXACT length equation, which forces the bvar to be the LAST argument — that is the only thing the equation buys, and it is exactly what excludes the over-applied case. A slot invariant buys the same locating power and is STABLE UNDER APPENDING, which the equation is not. It is also what iota_reduct actually reads. \\
\\
Nine of the eleven arms got SIMPLER than the length-pinned original, because the invariant is stated on the source's own head rather than on a decomposition: beta no longer needs app_inj_fst, and iota/delta need no transports. All the new cost is in the app arm, which splits on nat_lt_le_dichotomy and calls the existing boundary lemma verbatim below the slot. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_BVAR_SLOT_STAR_PRESERVED,
            "bvar_slot_star_preserved: and any number of steps. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_IOTA_IMMUNE_OF_BVAR_SLOT,
            "iota_immune_of_bvar_slot: the generalisation of iota_immune_of_bvar_major to ARBITRARY spine length. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_IOTA_NEUTRAL_OF_BVAR_SLOT,
            "iota_neutral_of_bvar_slot: chained up the spine, mixing with iota_neutral_of_under_applied below the slot. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_NF_HEAD_APP_OF_BVAR_SLOT,
            "nf_head_app_of_bvar_slot: nf_head at an over-applied recursor spine with a bvar in the major slot. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_HNF3_APP_RESIDUAL_OF_OVER_APPLIED_BVAR_SLOT,
            "hnf3_app_residual_of_over_applied_bvar_slot: the residual, supplied for the OVER-APPLIED bvar-slot class — the class stuck_recursor.rs records as what remains. \\
\\
Note what this does NOT do: it does not discharge over_res at its stated type. over_res constrains only the SPINE — dead recursor head, length past the major — and never names what sits in the major slot. nf_head's only usable arm there wants iota_immune, a statement over ALL reducts, and every in-tree supplier of that works by exhibiting a SYNTACTIC invariant on the major. With the major arbitrary the only handle is wh3_stuck_at, which speaks about ONE step at ONE budget. So over_res is strictly HARDER than bnd_res, which at least pins its major. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        self.add_recursive_def(
            SRC_NF_HEAD_NATREC_OVER_APPLIED_WITNESS,
            "nf_head_natrec_over_applied_witness (NON-VACUITY): a five-argument Nat.rec spine at the real reflected environment, bvar at slot 3, one trailing argument. Every hypothesis is Eq.refl or Le.refl — it either computes or it does not elaborate. DerivedProved, zero axiom_deps.",
        )?;
        Ok(())
    }
}

